<section class="panel chapter" data-surface="board" data-ruler>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="chapter__tag"><span class="util">Chapter</span><%= num('I') %></p>
    <p class="chapter__word d-xl">About</p>
    <div class="grid chapter__body">
      <div class="chapter__art" data-io><%= doodle(:capsule, "A child's drawing of a medicine capsule, an arrow, and a pencil.") %></div>
      <div class="chapter__text">
        <h1 class="chapter__h">From pharmacist to learning designer.</h1>
        <p class="r-l">I'm Pratima Jain, a learning experience designer and project lead at Tata Consultancy Services (TCS) in Mumbai. I trained as a pharmacist, and for more than nine years I have helped life sciences teams learn.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sheet" data-surface="chalk" data-ruler>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid story reveal" data-io>
      <h2 class="d-m g-l">How I got here</h2>
      <div class="g-r prose r-l">
        <p>I discovered my love for learning and for training people at the Youth Trainer's Academy in 2013, and again while coordinating training for the International Pharmaceutical Students' Federation. I was studying pharmacy and management at the time, but I already knew I wanted to work in learning and development.</p>
        <p>The chance came earlier than I expected. I began my career in scientific marketing. When my first employer closed its India office in 2017, I took it as my opening and joined TCS as a trainer. I have been in learning ever since.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid story reveal" data-io>
      <h2 class="d-m g-l">A learning engineer in the making</h2>
      <div class="g-r prose r-l">
        <p>A learning engineer builds AI agents, software and automations so that people don't have to learn the task in the first place. Take a firm that needs flyers in its own brand style. I would rather build it a marketing coach that knows the brand guidelines than teach everyone graphic design.</p>
        <p>It is the shortest possible route to the business objective, with the human touch and the learning process still at the heart of it. I'm getting there one experiment at a time, which is why I call myself a <span class="highlight">learning engineer in the making</span>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sheet" data-surface="chalk" data-ruler>
  <div class="wrap">
    <%= index_list('At TCS', [
      row('Project Lead', 'Sep 2024 to now', 'I design e-learning, videos and documents, lead the team and work with clients directly. I look after timelines, communication and quality.'),
      row('Instructional Designer', 'Oct 2018 to now', 'Needs analysis, storyboards and reviewing development work, on my own and leading teams of 1 to 20 people.'),
      row('Technical Trainer', 'Apr 2017 to Sep 2018', "Pharmaceutical products and therapeutic area trainer in the Pharma Academy of Learning and Sharing, the academy for TCS's life sciences business. I trained 200+ participants across 40+ trainings on pharmaceutical drugs.")
    ], cls: 'index--path') %>
    <%= index_list('Before TCS', [
      row('Management Trainee, Besins Healthcare', 'Jun 2016 to Mar 2017', 'Scientific marketing of hormonal products, including customer engagement programmes.'),
      row('Training Co-ordinator, IPSF', 'Sep 2015 to Aug 2016', "Organised Trainers' Development Camps and international Leaders in Training programmes."),
      row('Intern, Piramal Enterprises', 'Jan to Mar 2016'),
      row('Summer Intern, Piramal Pharma Solutions', 'May to Aug 2015', 'Analysis, segmentation and targeting of the sterile injectable market.')
    ], cls: 'index--path') %>
    <%= index_list('Education', [
      row('B.Pharm + MBA (Pharm. Tech.), NMIMS', '2011 to 2016', 'Pharma Management.'),
      row("Youth Trainer's Academy", '2013', 'A train-the-trainer programme by Zero Generation, where I learnt to structure and deliver training.')
    ]) %>
    <%= index_list('Community', [
      row('The Candle Project', 'Since 2017', 'Volunteer English trainer.'),
      row('Ayuda', 'Since 2013', 'Volunteer, working with children.'),
      row('Lean In Mumbai', 'Eight years', 'Part of the community.')
    ]) %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sheet next" data-surface="chalk" data-ruler>
  <div class="wrap reveal" data-io>
    <p class="d-m">That is where I have been. This is what I think about.</p>
    <a class="link" href="<%= r('ideas/') %>">Read my ideas<%= arrow %></a>
  </div>
</section>
